e  same sort of intellectual playing field  as say  jing or paristan but in terms of combat  it's very hard to pinpoint a better  thinker and on-the-fly strategist but  most importantly of all moral does his  best to remain grounded at all times  in fact he is acutely aware that even  with all of these incredibly strong  features he could be defeated and  potentially even killed at a moment's  notice by a significantly less  experienced adversary simply due to  underestimating them and being surprised  by a weird nun ability and that thought  process is quite a rarity actually most  men users of morris caliber carry some  degree of arrogance or at the very least  far  far too much confidence with them into  battle whereas the name of marl's game  is versatility he is a man experienced  enough to know that anything is possible  in this world of our control and his  abilities reflect a desire to respond to  quite literally anything that gets  thrown his way  before launching into that though moral  is one of the very rare characters in  the series who provides us with an  accurate aura metric as according to  knuckle one of moral students he  possesses an aura pool consisting of  roughly 70  000 units what does units mean well  unfortunately it's a knuckle exclusive  measurement but it is consistent and  this can be directly compared to mr gone  who knuckle also measured in his  peak condition prior to the palace  invasion gone was capable of generating  twenty one and a half thousand units of  aura thus giving moral more than three  times the access to aura that an already  quite terrifying gone had  and the only thing that really  empirically eclipses morals aura  quantity is out of the royal guard the  ant king marawim and obviously isaac  netara although when trying to classify  them it's usually easier just to state  that their aura is effectively infinite  because their pools are just that  ridiculously large but all of that  really is to say that moral's aura  reserves are envious to say the least  and quite possibly his greatest  individual asset at most  as for someone who strives to be  prepared for anything and everything  a lot of leeway is going to be essential  in order to ensure that moral doesn't  lock himself into a dead end of or a  dedication now moving on tomorrow's  actual netfinity he happens to be a  natural manipulator which i think is  actually quite initially  counterproductive tomorrow's mission  with nenus i mean manipulation is  admittedly far more versatile than most  people give a credit for and that's  because when we think of this affinity  the mind always wanders to certain  characters like gillamy zoldick or  perhaps even  shalnok of house no last name both of  whom are the post children for pure  manipulation  in fact at no stage at any of their  abilities even credited with anything  else despite my insistence that emission  would be necessary in a couple of cases  but even if it was it would be a minimal  splash use of a mission and moral is  very much the exact opposite of this  when it comes to net moral investors  aura equally into three differing  affinities being manipulation emission  and transmutation which is a very  bizarre combination and extraordinarily  difficult to pull off but as a result  moro becomes a troublesome opponent and  nigh  on impossible to overcome which leads us  quite nicely into marl's crowning  nenability which is named deep purple  and the basic gist of this is that moral  is able to use his incredible quantity  of aura to create these smoke-based  constructs  which can take the form of items such as  ropes rafts grass like literally name  any  item any at all and maura will be able  to create it out of smoke but in  addition to that he can also create foe  nene beast by which i mean constructs  with the illusion of life that morrow  then goes on to manipulate  and this latter feature is probably what  most fans think of when it comes to  moral specifically his smoke troopers  however there is a pretty extraordinary  degree of confusion regarding how they  are brought into being which to get into  let's start with the smoke itself  because that presents a pretty big  problem  because this smoke is no smoke at all  it's actually transmuted aura which is  where a lot of the confusion surrounding  deep purple stems from the primary issue  being that moral as stated earlier is a  natural manipulator which if we examine  the nen ring  is generally incompatible with  transmutation due to them being in the  exact opposite positions so usually it  would be incredibly unwise for a  manipulator to try and dip into  transmutation because their aura cost  per mileage would be absolutely abysmal  and destructively inefficient  even for someone with morals ground  reserves however there is a surprisingly  simple way around this which is by  adding a restriction on the use of  transmutation and in moral's case that  would be the gigantic f  off pipe and in order to activate deep  purple or in fact any smoke-based  ability moro can only transmute aura  through this pipe via the process  of essentially smoking his own aura only  with that strict limitation can he use  transmutation to an efficient degree and  i would imagine that the size of the  pipe also plays greatly into these  limitations as well and if moral had say  an even bigger pipe then the  transmutation could be even more potent  however he went about as big as he  reasonably could to keep himself  versatile but i should mention that a  great misconception within many  hunthunter fans is that moral smoke is  just regular smoke that he goes on to  manipulate which to be fair does make  some straightforward sense with his  affinity as a manipulator but it's just  not true moral's aura smoke demonstrates  too many bizarre qualities that natural  smoke is simply not capable of for  example in his fight against leo moral  smoke is able to act as a solid  substance and form a series of  underwater pipes  and manipulation is just not capable of  such a thing you cannot manipulate  something to bend the laws of its  established reality  however what you can do is transmute an  entirely new substance that mimics smoke  whilst also providing other beneficial  features like how hisoka's bungee gum  contains the properties of both rubber  and gum there i said it and it is  neither substance yet both at the same  time all thanks to the power of  transmutation the best i could really  see one doing is coming up with an  explanation that moral uses real smoke  and then invokes enhancement on the  smoke to solidify and tighten the  particles or whatever which you know  isn't the most outrageous thing i've  ever seen or heard in hunt hunter  however it is a much more complicated  solution to a very simple nen problem  and in the end it doesn't matter anyway  because we do have confirmation when we  see morril's process of constructing a  smoke trooper so firstly what happens is  moral emits a ball of aura very standard  emission  almost exactly what someone like razer  would do except this ball is not meant  to serve an offensive purpose you could  think of it more like a computer chip or  some other programming device but this  aura nucleus is what moral issues  commands too which are then performed by  the smoke figure formed around it which  speaking of step two here has more quite  blatantly stating  then envelope it with smoke aura and i  really don't know how much clearer we  can get here here moral is stating that  his aura and the smoke are one in the  same thing so a transmuted substance  there is no other option which then goes  on to become the shape of whatever moral  wants to create and only then does  marl's primary affinity of manipulation  come into play which is then used to  issue commands to the aura nucleus  within it really is quite a genius level  use of none in my opinion because  manipulators and conjurers tend to get  quite screwed over in the world of hunt  hunter due to being right next to the  unusable specialization affinity which  is why a lot of conjurers and  manipulators will stick to more pure  based applications because of the  limited splash potential but morale just  took full advantage of the rules of men  deciding to take on a cumbersome but  workable restriction in order to have  access to an almost completely unique  skill set  there are further limitations though  specifically on deep purple and when it  comes to the smoke troopers moral has a  maximum capacity of crafting 216 of them  which yes is a hell of a lot but in this  case he is sacrificing quality for  quantity and it's really only useful  when he requires a show of overwhelming  force or for quick efficient scouting  purposes now alternatively morrow can  compress this number down to 50 troopers  which are capable of performing more  complex commands and they can even take  on more realistic forms  in fact to the untrained eye and even to  the trained end user they can pass for  living things because at this point even  an experienced nen user's end cannot  tell them apart from regular humans but  one problem that should also be  mentioned is that once moral has created  smoke troops or indeed smoke anything  his aura is then committed to that  construct and in order to retrieve the  aura spent he needs to dispel them which  can leave morrow quite compromised in  situations where deep purple is heavily  utilized although once again this  usually plays in tomorrow's great  advantage of our reserves he can very  much spend exorbitant amounts and still  have enough left to defend himself  quite effectively against well most  opponents anyway maybe not so much say a  member of the royal guard which brings  us to the second  and indeed final of marl's named  abilities actually which is known as  smokey jail  which at first glance just appears like  another unique use of deep purple but  the important technical difference is  that this ability does not utilize  emission it's just manipulation and  transmutation  coming together to form an unbreakable  barrier of smoke thing to encase someone  or something in  theoretically unbreakable anyway because  as it turns out due to transmuted smoke  still inherently possessing many of the  core qualities of smoke particle-sized  objects can still pass through the  barrier which is very awkward since  during the palace invasion moro was  faced with the one opponent who could do  exactly that it's still a ridiculously  powerful ability though however it may  come with at least one restriction being  that moral must also encase himself in  the smoky jail and it also likely  requires a truly massive investment of  aura to keep up due to there being  nothing but speculatory limitations  because it's just way way way way too  powerful to be used in a casual manner  and that's very much moral quite  possibly one of the most well-balanced  end users in hunter hunter someone whose  natural affinity of men did not  necessarily  agree with their path forward in life  and so someone who managed to use their  minds like no other because in theory  really moral is nothing all that special  we've seen stronger characters we've  seen smarter characters and we've  certainly seen more naturally talented  characters but moral makes his mark on  this world simply through hard work and  merit and really i think a lack of that  gone and killer  style talent may actually work very much  tomorrow's advantage because it has  forced him to think very creatively  about his various restrictions in life  resulting in one of the most captivating  nen users in the entire series but what  do you guys think please do leave your  thoughts in the comments below or even  join my discord server and if you're  keen for some more hunt on content then  please to go and check out some of my  other videos or even subscribe to the  channel for regular hunt on to glory  delivered straight into your youtube  feed but for now this has been the new  world review  and i'll see you next time

